# CVE-2026-39324 (GHSA-33qg-7wpp-89cq): Rack::Session::Cookie fell back to
# the unverified coder when decryption failed. In unpacked_cookie_data
# (lib/rack/session/cookie.rb), a cookie the configured encryptors
# could not decrypt left session_data nil, and the branch
#
#   elsif !session_data && coder
#     session_data = coder.decode(cookie_data)
#
# handed the raw cookie to the coder -- Base64::Marshal by default,
# whose decode runs ::Marshal.load(super(str)). A forged plain
# Base64::Marshal cookie therefore deserialized unauthenticated in
# any deployment that had configured :secrets (untrusted
# deserialization, CWE-502). The fixed revision (f43638c, the commit
# that names the advisory in releases.md) adds encryptors.empty? to
# the guard, so a deployment with encryptors rejects the cookie
# instead of falling back. The vulnerable construct is present at the
# parent and the remediation at the commit; no pool correction.
#
# ATTENTION, engine gap plus a configuration-shaped guard, rechecked.
#
# 1. The taint chain is intact except for one hop. request.cookies[@key]
#    is labelled code.HttpInput (cookie.rb:215) and ::Marshal.load is
#    labelled code.Deserialization (cookie.rb:110 and :153), but
#    coder.decode never resolves: Ruby dispatch reaches resolveTargets
#    with no receiver type (nothing records the type of
#    @coder = options[:coder] ||= Base64::Marshal.new -- an op-assign
#    hides the constructor call at the Assign case in lowering, and the
#    attr_reader spelling `coder` is not linked to the ivar), so the call
#    falls to the unique-method-name-across-program fallback, which
#    short-circuits ambiguous at the second same-named definition.
#    `decode` is defined in six classes in cookie.rb (Base64,
#    Base64::Marshal, Base64::JSON, Base64::ZipJSON, Identity, Marshal).
#    Re-measured on the real file: `vyql trace -from HttpInput -to
#    Deserialization` reports 0 reachable pairs and 8 dead-end sources;
#    the identical file with five of the six `def decode` renamed
#    reports 2 reachable pairs, cookie.rb:215 -> cookie.rb:110 in 6
#    hops. The first two tests below pin that pair.
# 2. The guard the fixed revision adds is runtime configuration, not dataflow.
#    With the ambiguity removed (single decode definition), the
#    patched form `elsif !session_data && encryptors.empty? && coder`
#    still reports VYQL-DESER-001 critical from the cookie -- measured
#    directly, not assumed, and pinned by the third test below. The
#    encryptors.empty? the fix leaves inside the guarded method is this
#    library's own attr_reader, so a core.SafeDeserialization binding
#    keyed on it would be this patch's own vocabulary rather than
#    anything derivable from the documentation, and a broad check
#    concept would clear unrelated deserialization findings besides.
#    Same family as the configuration-side fixes at 1514/1535/1540/
#    1556/1557/1593.
#
# On the real tree at f43638c^ the scan reports 10 findings (2 x
# VYQL-DESER-001 critical, 3 x VYQL-INJ-023, 2 x VYQL-CRY-003,
# 3 x VYQL-CRY-001), byte-identical over three --cache off runs at the
# parent and three at the fix, and identical between the revisions: the
# Marshal.load rows source from library.param-source (the decode
# parameter itself), not the cookie, and the one review flag
# (code.ObjectLookupByUserInput) sits in a test file. When Ruby
# receiver types land, test two starts reporting and must be
# re-measured against the real revisions; test three already reports,
# so the guard it names is the reason a resolution fix alone converts
# nothing.
# verify_current_expected: attention-engine-gap, both revisions report.

test "rack session cookie fallback: a unique coder decode reports the unverified deserialization"
  lang ruby
  file lib/rack/session/cookie.rb
  expect VYQL-DESER-001
  code
  ```
  class Coder
    def decode(str)
      Marshal.load(super(str)) rescue nil
    end
  end

  class Session
    attr_reader :coder

    def initialize(options = {})
      @coder = options[:coder] ||= Coder.new
    end

    def unpacked_cookie_data(request)
      if cookie_data = request.cookies["rack.session"]
        session_data = coder.decode(cookie_data)
      end
      session_data || {}
    end
  end
  ```

test "rack session cookie fallback: a second decode definition silences the chain"
  lang ruby
  file lib/rack/session/cookie.rb
  reject VYQL-DESER-001
  code
  ```
  class CoderBase
    def decode(str)
      Base64.decode64(str)
    end
  end

  class Coder < CoderBase
    def decode(str)
      Marshal.load(super(str)) rescue nil
    end
  end

  class Session
    attr_reader :coder

    def initialize(options = {})
      @coder = options[:coder] ||= Coder.new
    end

    def unpacked_cookie_data(request)
      if cookie_data = request.cookies["rack.session"]
        session_data = coder.decode(cookie_data)
      end
      session_data || {}
    end
  end
  ```

test "rack session cookie fallback: the fixed revision's encryptors.empty? guard does not clear the report"
  lang ruby
  file lib/rack/session/cookie.rb
  expect VYQL-DESER-001
  code
  ```
  class Coder
    def decode(str)
      Marshal.load(super(str)) rescue nil
    end
  end

  class Encryptor
    def decrypt(data)
      raise "invalid message"
    end
  end

  class Session
    attr_reader :coder, :encryptors

    def initialize(options = {})
      @encryptors = [Encryptor.new]
      @coder = options[:coder] ||= Coder.new
    end

    def unpacked_cookie_data(request)
      if cookie_data = request.cookies["rack.session"]
        session_data = nil
        encryptors.each do |encryptor|
          begin
            session_data = encryptor.decrypt(cookie_data)
            break
          rescue
            next
          end
        end
        if !session_data && encryptors.empty? && coder
          session_data = coder.decode(cookie_data)
        end
      end
      session_data || {}
    end
  end
  ```
